From: NixOS maintainers <maintainers@nixos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: compiler: undefine __attribute_const__ before linux/types.h

glibc 2.42 defines __attribute_const__ in sys/cdefs.h.  The tools header
tools/include/linux/compiler.h defines an empty __attribute_const__ stub
at line 122, then includes linux/types.h at line 157, which transitively
pulls in sys/cdefs.h.  GCC 15 treats the redefinition as -Werror.

Undefine the stub immediately before the types.h include so glibc's
definition is the first (and only) definition, eliminating the conflict.

--- a/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
+++ b/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
@@ -153,7 +153,12 @@
 #ifndef unlikely
 # define unlikely(x)		__builtin_expect(!!(x), 0)
 #endif
 
+/* glibc 2.42 defines __attribute_const__ in <sys/cdefs.h>, pulled in
+ * transitively by <linux/types.h> below.  Undefine our empty stub so
+ * glibc can provide the real definition without a GCC 15 -Wredefined error. */
+#undef __attribute_const__
+
 #include <linux/types.h>
 
 /*
